;; java.nio.file (doc/classes/JAVA-DEFERRED-TRIAGE.md, F9, "As built: F9 (write-ahead)"; the user's decision of
;; 2026-11-07): jdk26u's own java.nio.file, .attribute and .spi with the default provider of Linux, sun.nio.fs's Unix
;; and Linux classes, in place of jrt's own Path, Files and HostPath (removed). Their natives are jrt's Go
;; (go/arbace/jrt/nio_fs_linux.ae: UnixNativeDispatcher.c's, LinuxNativeDispatcher.c's, LinuxWatchService.c's and
;; UnixFileSystem.c's), over native memory (go/arbace/jrt/nativemem.ae: NativeBuffer's addresses). jrt's overlays
;; (overlay/jdk/java.base, derived from jdk26u's files by .tmp/f9/derive.py's asserted replacements): Files,
;; FileSystems, FileChannelLinesSpliterator, spi/FileSystemProvider (no ServiceLoader, no VM, no JavaLangAccess's
;; coding: jdk.internal.jrt.NioStrings), UnixNativeDispatcher, LinuxNativeDispatcher and LinuxWatchService (no
;; library; UnixException's factory registered), UnixFileSystem (the buffered copy through a NativeBuffer),
;; UnixChannelFactory (the descriptor adopted by jrt's file table, jdk.internal.jrt.HostFiles.adopt), UnixPath,
;; NativeBuffer (no Cleaner), NativeBuffers (a plain ThreadLocal), UnixUserDefinedFileAttributeView (no
;; JavaNioAccess). jdk26u's FileChannel again (F7's overlay, whose open asked jrt's FileChannelImpl, removed): open
;; asks the provider. What stays outside the world in members (the asynchronous file channel, the installed
