;; The JCA's tail (doc/classes/JAVA-DEFERRED-TRIAGE.md, "As built: F23 (write-ahead)"): classes F1's
;; closure left out that the providers name by string, so no import scan found them:
;; SunJCE's AlgorithmParameters.GCM, sun.security.util.GCMParameters (Cipher.getParameters of
;; every AES/GCM cipher; constructed by jrt's JceServices), and DRBG's CTR_DRBG mechanism,
;; sun.security.provider.CtrDrbg (DRBG.createImpl's third branch; a DrbgParameters or
;; securerandom.drbg.config naming CTR_DRBG); and MD4, the digest no provider lists that
;; MD4.getInstance gives through a provider of its own (NTLM's, SASL's below; constructed by jrt's
;; JrtServices).
