;; SASL (doc/classes/JAVA-DEFERRED-TRIAGE.md, "As built: F23 (write-ahead)"; JCS133 (a): Kerberos and
;; GSS-API by design, SASL deferred until F1 and F4 were in): jdk26u's java.security.sasl, the API
;; (javax.security.sasl) and the SunSASL provider's mechanisms (com.sun.security.sasl: CRAM-MD5,
;; DIGEST-MD5, EXTERNAL, PLAIN, NTLM), translated into java.base's tree as java.logging's are (KIND
;; share:java.security.sasl), with java.base's NTLM implementation (com.sun.security.ntlm) the NTLM
;; mechanism uses. SunSASL constructs its factories itself (its Provider.Service subclass), so only
;; ProviderConfig's variant names it (overlay/jdk/variants/ProviderConfig.ae; ProviderConfigSasl.ae until JCS232 (a)); the GSSAPI mechanism
;; (jdk.security.jgss's JdkSASL) stays out with GSS-API.
(def sasl-sources
  "SASL in the Go build (F23): paths relative to jdk26u."
  (vec (sort
         (concat
           (map #(str "src/java.security.sasl/share/classes/javax/security/sasl/" % ".java")
                ["AuthenticationException" "AuthorizeCallback" "RealmCallback" "RealmChoiceCallback"
                 "Sasl" "SaslClient" "SaslClientFactory" "SaslException" "SaslServer"
                 "SaslServerFactory"])
           (map #(str "src/java.security.sasl/share/classes/com/sun/security/sasl/" % ".java")
                ["ClientFactoryImpl" "CramMD5Base" "CramMD5Client" "CramMD5Server" "ExternalClient"
                 "PlainClient" "Provider" "ServerFactoryImpl"
                 "digest/DigestMD5Base" "digest/DigestMD5Client" "digest/DigestMD5Server"
                 "digest/FactoryImpl" "digest/SecurityCtx"
                 "ntlm/FactoryImpl" "ntlm/NTLMClient" "ntlm/NTLMServer"
                 "util/AbstractSaslImpl" "util/PolicyUtils"])
           (map #(str "src/java.base/share/classes/com/sun/security/ntlm/" % ".java")
                ["Client" "NTLM" "NTLMException" "Server" "Version"])
           ;; and JAAS's LDAP principal (jdk.security.auth, beside F4's principals): an LdapName,
           ;; F19's, with no directory behind it
           ["src/jdk.security.auth/share/classes/com/sun/security/auth/LdapPrincipal.java"]))))

(def jmx-sources
  "JMX's core in the Go build (JCS263, the user's decision of 2026-11-08 reversing JCS95 (a) for it;
  doc/classes/JAVA-DEFERRED-TRIAGE.md, \"As built: JMX-1 (write-ahead)\"): paths relative to jdk26u, files of
  src/java.management translated as java.base's. javax.management's API (the MBean server, its factory and
  builder, the standard and dynamic MBeans, MXBeans, notifications, queries, descriptors), its open data
  (openmbean), its loader repository (loading) and its timer service (timer); the reference implementation
  com.sun.jmx.mbeanserver (the introspectors, the MXBean mappings over java.lang.reflect's generics, F25's),
  com.sun.jmx.interceptor and com.sun.jmx.defaults, and of com.sun.jmx.remote.util the two helpers the server
  names (EnvHelp, ClassLogger). Not the connectors (javax.management.remote and com.sun.jmx.remote's rest: RMI,
  JCS132), the model, monitor and relation services (no test of the measure asks them). jdk26u's ObjectName and
  CompositeData replace F13's skeletons; sun.management's MemoryUsageCompositeData and LazyCompositeData give
