(def rmi-sources
  "Java RMI in the Go build (JCS255 (b), the user's decision of 2026-11-08; doc/classes/JAVA-DEFERRED-TRIAGE.md,
  \"As built: F27 (write-ahead)\"): paths relative to jdk26u, files of src/java.rmi/share/classes translated as
  java.base's: java.rmi's API (the exceptions, MarshalledObject, Naming), java.rmi.server (the remote objects and
  references, UnicastRemoteObject, RMIClassLoader, the socket factories, RemoteObjectInvocationHandler: the dynamic
  stubs over JCS170's Proxy), java.rmi.registry and java.rmi.dgc; sun.rmi's runtime: the unicast references and their
  marshal streams over jdk26u's object streams (JCS167), the transport over TCP (F10a's sockets), the object table,
  the distributed garbage collector (DGCImpl, DGCClient over java.lang.ref's queues) and the registry (RegistryImpl
  with its stub and skeleton); javax.rmi.ssl's socket factories over F3's SunJSSE. Not here: sun.rmi.log (the
  activation daemon's log, removed with activation in JDK 17: nothing else uses it) and RMISecurityManager (a
  SecurityManager, which the Go build has not). jrt's own beside them (overlay/jdk): RMIClassLoader (no ServiceLoader),
  sun.rmi.transport.GC (librmi not loaded; its native maxObjectInspectionAge jrt's, go/arbace/jrt/rmi.ae) and DGCClient
  (its references' entries weak, jrt has no PhantomReference), sun.rmi.runtime.Log (the caller's frame from a Throwable's
  stack trace, no StackWalker) and RuntimeUtil (no thread groups) derived from jdk26u's by test/jrt/derive.ae."
  (vec (sort
         (concat
           (map #(str "src/java.rmi/share/classes/java/rmi/" % ".java")
                ["AccessException" "AlreadyBoundException" "ConnectException" "ConnectIOException" "MarshalException"
                 "MarshalledObject" "Naming" "NoSuchObjectException" "NotBoundException" "RMISecurityException"
                 "Remote" "RemoteException" "ServerError" "ServerException" "ServerRuntimeException"
                 "StubNotFoundException" "UnexpectedException" "UnknownHostException" "UnmarshalException"])
           ;; the error the rmic stubs' static initializers throw when a remote method is missing (java.base's)
           ["src/java.base/share/classes/java/lang/NoSuchMethodError.java"]
           (map #(str "src/java.rmi/share/classes/java/rmi/dgc/" % ".java")
                ["DGC" "Lease" "VMID"])
           (map #(str "src/java.rmi/share/classes/java/rmi/registry/" % ".java")
                ["LocateRegistry" "Registry" "RegistryHandler"])
           (map #(str "src/java.rmi/share/classes/java/rmi/server/" % ".java")
                ["ExportException" "LoaderHandler" "LogStream" "ObjID" "Operation" "RMIClassLoaderSpi" "RMIClientSocketFactory" "RMIFailureHandler" "RMIServerSocketFactory"
                 "RMISocketFactory" "RemoteCall" "RemoteObject" "RemoteObjectInvocationHandler" "RemoteRef"
                 "RemoteServer" "RemoteStub" "ServerCloneException" "ServerNotActiveException" "ServerRef" "Skeleton"
                 "SkeletonMismatchException" "SkeletonNotFoundException" "SocketSecurityException" "UID"
                 "UnicastRemoteObject" "Unreferenced"])
           (map #(str "src/java.rmi/share/classes/javax/rmi/ssl/" % ".java")
                ["SslRMIClientSocketFactory" "SslRMIServerSocketFactory"])
           (map #(str "src/java.rmi/share/classes/sun/rmi/registry/" % ".java")
                ["RegistryImpl" "RegistryImpl_Skel" "RegistryImpl_Stub"])
           (map #(str "src/java.rmi/share/classes/sun/rmi/server/" % ".java")
                ["DeserializationChecker" "Dispatcher" "LoaderHandler" "MarshalInputStream" "MarshalOutputStream"
                 "UnicastRef" "UnicastRef2" "UnicastServerRef" "UnicastServerRef2" "Util" "WeakClassHashMap"])
           (map #(str "src/java.rmi/share/classes/sun/rmi/transport/" % ".java")
                ["Channel" "Connection" "ConnectionInputStream" "ConnectionOutputStream" "DGCAckHandler"
                 "DGCImpl" "DGCImpl_Skel" "DGCImpl_Stub" "Endpoint" "LiveRef" "ObjectEndpoint" "ObjectTable"
                 "StreamRemoteCall" "Target" "Transport" "TransportConstants" "WeakRef"])
           (map #(str "src/java.rmi/share/classes/sun/rmi/transport/tcp/" % ".java")
                ["TCPChannel" "TCPConnection" "TCPDirectSocketFactory" "TCPEndpoint" "TCPTransport"])))))

(def jmx-remote-sources
  "JMX's remote connectors in the Go build (JMX-2, F27: JCS284's connectors, with RMI, JCS255 (b); doc/classes/
  JAVA-DEFERRED-TRIAGE.md, \"As built: F27 (write-ahead)\"): paths relative to jdk26u, files of src/java.management
  and src/java.management.rmi translated as java.base's: javax.management.remote's API (the connector and server
  interfaces, JMXServiceURL, the notifications, the subject delegation permission), com.sun.jmx.remote's internals (the
  notification buffers and forwarders, the communicator admins), security (the access controllers, the file login
  module, the password manager) and util (the class loader orderings); java.management.rmi's RMI connector and server
  (RMIConnectorServer, RMIJRMPServerImpl, RMIConnectionImpl with their rmic stubs, ProxyRef, RMIExporter, the providers).
  jrt's own beside them (overlay/jdk): JMXConnectorFactory and JMXConnectorServerFactory (their providers
  jdk.internal.jrt.JmxProviders', no ServiceLoader), ClientCommunicatorAdmin, ServerCommunicatorAdmin and
  ClientNotifForwarder (no thread groups), RMIConnector (no class defined from bytes) derived from jdk26u's by
  test/jrt/derive.ae, and jdk.internal.jrt.JmxProviders. Not here: NoCallStackClassLoader (what RMIConnector's
  derivation no longer makes)."
  (vec (sort
         (concat
